# Environment
# `.env.*` catches every sidecar — .env.local, .env.ota.local, and the ad-hoc
# backups that turn up mid-session. The old rules listed variants by name, so a
# file like `.env.claude-bak` was untracked but NOT ignored, and one `git add -A`
# away from committing the App Check debug tokens it holds. A registered token
# mints valid App Check tokens and bypasses App Attest and Play Integrity, so
# this is a real secret, not a config.
# `.env.example` is the schema, carries no values, and is tracked on purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc

